+    <owner>/<Repo> <sha> pins <file>, <file>.     cicd.writeVersionPins, branch main
+    <owner>/<Repo> <sha> pushed to prd.           Promote-PRD
+    <owner>/<Repo> already carries these pins: nothing committed, nothing pushed.
+    <owner>/<Repo> <sha> already on prd: nothing pushed.
+
+The first two pushed a commit, so there is a sync to wait for. An Application
+follows one when a source of it tracks that repo and branch and, for a pin line,
+its helm ``valueFiles`` name a pinned file. It has rolled the commit when Argo CD
+reports it ``Synced`` at the commit or a descendant, with no sync running and its
+health not ``Progressing``. The last two pushed nothing: each matched app's
+current state is reported, not waited on.
+
+Argo CD is read from the Kubernetes API with ``~/.kube/config`` (context
+``prd``, namespace ``argocd-prd``), read-only. Git questions are asked only of the
+environment's own clone of the deploy repo, ``/work/<Repo>``, fetched first.
